      "words": 1245,
      "summary": null,
      "keywords": [],
      "extract": "Chapter 1. Introduction 1. Introduction 1.1 Background International human rights law includes fundamental commitments of states to enable women and adolescent girls to survive pregnancy and childbirth as part of their enjoyment of sexual and reproductive health and rights and living a life of dignity (1). The World Health Organization (WHO) envisions a world where “every pregnant woman and newborn receives quality",
